    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3490"
                            type="person">Mr. Hofman</rs>
                        <lb/>Columbia Management Corporation <lb/>551 Fifth Avenue <lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York
                            City</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-05-11">May 11,
                        1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3490" type="person">Mr.
                        Hofman</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>A few weeks ago I sent you a letter from <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3491"
                        type="person">Mr. Dayton</rs> telling me that he intends to continue the
                    personal reliability insurance of my predecessor in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__769" type="place">East Hampton</rs>. I asked you
                    whether this was the same insurance you intended to give me. Today I have
                    received the enclosed letter and policy. Now it seems as if there are two
                    different policies of which yours is more expensive than that of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3491" type="person">Mr. Dayton</rs>. Please let me
                    know by telephone or letter what you suggest me to do.</p>
                <closer><salute>Cordially yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
